<div class="step"><span class="name">drop_ratio</span><span class="eq">=</span>V_drop/V_line<span class="eq">=</span><span class="subst">4.79348 V/(230 V)</span><span class="eq">=</span><span class="result">0.0208412</span></div>
<h2 class="prose">What stays prose</h2>
<p class="prose">The subset is closed. Three things are outside it on purpose, and this is what they look like when a worksheet writes them:</p>
<p class="prose">The three dashes on the next line are text, not a rule. --- There are no thematic breaks and no setext headings, because `' --- resources ---` is what opens the resource trailer and a worksheet must not acquire a section break by writing about a range of values.</p>
<p class="prose">Leading whitespace is a wrap and not a code block, so a line indented like this one joins the line above it.</p>
<p class="prose">#3 is a screw size rather than a heading, because a heading needs a space after its marker.</p>
<p class="prose">A backslash protects a marker that was meant literally, so the line below is prose rather than a one-item list:</p>
